Subject: Raise frontend packages to patched releases

Origin: DHI-internal (the packaged UI must not keep the older library releases)
CVE: CVE-2026-49356
CVE: CVE-2026-53550
CVE: CVE-2026-59869
CVE: CVE-2026-73088
CVE: CVE-2026-73089
CVE: CVE-2026-84375
Advisory: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj
Description: Move js-yaml to 4.3.2, browserslist to 4.29.4, and @babel/core to 7.29.7 in the frozen bun lock. Upstream 0.21.1 already resolves valibot 1.5.0, so that library is not part of this patch. Bun has no bump step, so the lockfile is the edit.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/henrygd/beszel.git e2ed147a5aa6472e6462521632ccc7101668132c
Regenerate: `bun update --lockfile-only --cwd internal/site js-yaml@4.3.2 browserslist@4.29.4 @babel/core@7.29.7`
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/henrygd-beszel/tests -count=1 -run TestHubServes` expect "ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream can take these releases on its own schedule; this package pins them now)
Drop-When: dependency js-yaml >= 4.3.2 (browserslist >= 4.28.7 and @babel/core >= 7.29.6 are in the same lock edit)

The production install catalogs these libraries. The published ranges already allow the patched releases, and the lock stays frozen, so this patch is the only edit.

